வண்காற்","parts":[{"text":"வண்காற்","lemma":"வண்கால்","gloss":"strong post"}],"gloss":"strong post"},{"surface":"பந்தர்","parts":[{"text":"பந்தர்","lemma":"பந்தல்","gloss":"bower"}],"gloss":"bower"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"இடையன்","parts":[{"text":"இடையன்","lemma":"இடையன்","gloss":"shepherd"}],"gloss":"shepherd"},{"surface":"பொத்திய","parts":[{"text":"பொத்திய","lemma":"பொத்து","gloss":"kindled"}],"gloss":"kindled"},{"surface":"சிறுதீ","parts":[{"text":"சிறுதீ","lemma":"சிறுதீ","gloss":"small fire"}],"gloss":"small fire"},{"surface":"விளக்கத்துப்","parts":[{"text":"விளக்கத்துப்","lemma":"விளக்கத்து","gloss":"of the lamp"}],"gloss":"of the lamp"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பாணரொடு","parts":[{"text":"பாணரொடு","lemma":"பாணரொடு","gloss":"with the bards"}],"gloss":"with the bards"},{"surface":"இருந்த","parts":[{"text":"இருந்த","lemma":"இரு","gloss":"who sat"}],"gloss":"who sat"},{"surface":"நாணுடை","parts":[{"text":"நாணுடை","lemma":"நாணுடை","gloss":"possessing honor"}],"gloss":"possessing honor"},{"surface":"நெடுந்தகை","parts":[{"text":"நெடுந்தகை","lemma":"நெடுந்தகை","gloss":"noble man"}],"gloss":"noble man"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"வலம்படு","parts":[{"text":"வலம்படு","lemma":"வலம்படு","gloss":"victorious"}],"gloss":"victorious"},{"surface":"தானை","parts":[{"text":"தானை","lemma":"தானை","gloss":"army"}],"gloss":"army"},{"surface":"வேந்தற்கு","parts":[{"text":"வேந்தற்கு","lemma":"வேந்தன்","gloss":"to the king"}],"gloss":"to the king"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"உலந்துழி","parts":[{"text":"உலந்துழி","lemma":"உலந்துழி","gloss":"when perished"}],"gloss":"when perished"},{"surface":"உலக்கும்","parts":[{"text":"உலக்கும்","lemma":"உல","gloss":"will perish"}],"gloss":"will perish"},{"surface":"நெஞ்சறி","parts":[{"text":"நெஞ்சறி","lemma":"நெஞ்சறி","gloss":"heart-knowing"}],"gloss":"heart-knowing"},{"surface":"துணையே","parts":[{"text":"துணையே","lemma":"துணை","gloss":"companion"}],"gloss":"companion"}]}],"literal":"Wild cat male-like startled look soft-headed / bird-flesh eaten stench-smelling wide mouth / white-mouthed hunters' beloved companion children / small-leaved umbrella-thorn's hollow-socketed white thorn / reed-grass fine-shaft fitted arrow / slender-branch strong bow to bend drawing / cotton fence's bandicoot rat watching / dry land surrounding beautiful settlement small village's / kumizh-fruit eating white wide-mouthed turned / white-flowers spread strong-legged bower / shepherd kindled small fire light's / with bards sat possessing-honor noble man / victorious army king's / when perished perishing heart-knowing companion.","translation":"The children of the white-mouthed hunters, who have soft heads and startled looks like male wild cats, and wide mouths smelling of the bird-flesh they have eaten, draw their strong bows made of slender branches to bend, fitting arrows with fine shafts of reed-grass and white thorns from the hollow sockets of the small-leaved umbrella-thorn tree, and watch for bandicoot rats near the cotton fences. In that small village of beautiful homes surrounded by dry lands, under a strong-legged bower spread with white flowers, by the light of a small fire kindled by a shepherd, sits the honorable noble man with his bards. He is a heart-knowing companion to the king of the victorious army, who will perish when the king perishes.","modern":"காட்டுப் பூனையின் ஆண் போன்ற மிரண்ட பார்வையையும், பறவை இறைச்சியைத் தின்றதால் புலால் நாற்றம் வீசும் அகன்ற வாயையும் உடைய வெள்வாய் வேட்டுவர்களின் பிள்ளைகள், சிறிய இலைகளைக் கொண்ட உடை மரத்தின் துளையுள்ள முட்களையும் நாணல் தண்டுகளையும் கொண்டு தொடுத்த அம்புகளை, வளைந்த வில்லில் பூட்டி, பருத்தி வேலியருகே இருக்கும் பெருச்சாளிகளைப் பிடிக்கக் காத்திருக்கிறார்கள். புன்புலத்தைச் சார்ந்த அழகிய குடிகளைக் கொண்ட அந்தச் சீறூரில், குமிழம்பழங்களை உண்ணும் வெள்ளாடுகள் கட்டப்பட்ட, வெண்மையான வள்ளை மலர்கள் படர்ந்த, வலிய கால்களைக் கொண்ட பந்தலின் கீழ், இடையன் மூட்டிய சிறு நெருப்பின் வெளிச்சத்தில், பாணர்களோடு அமர்ந்திருக்கிறான் மானமும் பெருந்தகையும் உடைய தலைவன். அவன், வெற்றி பொருந்திய படையையுடைய வேந்தனுக்கு, அவன் அழியும் போது தானும் அழியும் நெஞ்சறிந்த உற்ற துணையாவான்.","explanation":"This poem belongs to the Puram genre, specifically the theme of 'Vallāṇ Mullai' (the strength and valor of a warrior in the Mullai landscape). The poet Alathur Kizhar describes a small, dry-land village (Seerur) where the children of hunters are already skilled in archery, hunting bandicoot rats near cotton fences with makeshift arrows. In this humble setting, under a bower lit by a shepherd's small fire, sits a noble warrior sharing food and space with wandering bards. Despite his humble surroundings, this warrior is the ultimate loyal companion to the great king, ready to lay down his life when the king's life is lost. The imagery of the children's early mastery of weapons reflects the inherent martial valor of the community, highlighting the theme of loyalty and bravery.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}